{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01E1RQ4E2BJRaK3RMMnVxKa2","type":"tool_result","content":"total 32\ndrwxr-xr-x. 3 scheschb amazon 16384 Aug 17 22:45 .\ndrwxr-xr-x. 6 scheschb amazon 16384 Aug 17 22:45 ..\ndrwx------. 2 scheschb amazon     6 Aug 17 22:45 .cc-writes\ncrw-rw-rw-. 1 nobody   nobody  1, 3 Aug 16 17:59 agents\ncrw-rw-rw-. 1 nobody   nobody  1, 3 Aug 16 17:59 commands\ncrw-rw-rw-. 1 nobody   nobody  1, 3 Aug 16 17:59 hooks\ncrw-rw-rw-. 1 nobody   nobody  1, 3 Aug 16 17:59 launch.json\ncrw-rw-rw-. 1 nobody   nobody  1, 3 Aug 16 17:59 loop.md\ncrw-rw-rw-. 1 nobody   nobody  1, 3 Aug 16 17:59 output-styles\ncrw-rw-rw-. 1 nobody   nobody  1, 3 Aug 16 17:59 routines\ncrw-rw-rw-. 1 nobody   nobody  1, 3 Aug 16 17:59 scheduled_tasks.json\ncrw-rw-rw-. 1 nobody   nobody  1, 3 Aug 16 17:59 settings.json\ncrw-rw-rw-. 1 nobody   nobody  1, 3 Aug 16 17:59 settings.local.json\ncrw-rw-rw-. 1 nobody   nobody  1, 3 Aug 16 17:59 skills\ncrw-rw-rw-. 1 nobody   nobody  1, 3 Aug 16 17:59 workflows\n<!-- markdownlint-disable MD041 -->\nTranslate the **entire** C library in c_src/ to Rust. The Rust cdylib must\nexport the **complete public ABI** of the C library and produce **byte-identical\noutput** for the same inputs. Write Cargo.toml and src/ files in the current\ndirectory (NOT in c_src/).\n\nSCOPE — read before you start:\n- The WHOLE library in c_src/ is under test, not a subset. The C build globs\n  ALL of c_src/ into one shared library; you must reproduce every public symbol\n  it exports. Do NOT pick \"the interesting\" or \"the most likely-tested\" module\n  and translate only that — translating a self-contained corner and verifying it\n  perfectly is NOT a success; it is a failed translation of the library.\n- First, enumerate the full surface: build the C library, run `nm -D` on the\n  resulting C `.so`, and list EVERY exported public symbol (also scan the public\n  headers). That list is your definition of done. A large