{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_kbbmpk7gex5nwlhwctcm7ugwwnrulry5g6m4jf67k46icda6ni7q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Summary\n\n**The library** (`c_src/`) is a single 43-line translation unit exporting exactly two symbols: `int static_sum(int)` (a running total kept in a function-local `static int sum`) and `void driver(int stride)` (prints `static_sum(i*stride)` for `i = 0..9` via `printf(\"%d\\n\", …)`).\n\n### Phase A — artifacts created (crate root)\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — `nm -D` inventory. C exports `static_sum`, `driver`; Rust exports both. **Symbol diff is empty**; nothing was missing, nothing stubbed. All Rust undefined symbols are libc/unwind imports.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 14 rows. Greps prove the C has an *empty* rejection surface: no `if`/`switch` at all, no `assert`, no `NULL`, no `errno`, no error sentinel, no pointer or length parameters. Rows therefore enumerate the boundary/degenerate inputs C accepts that would make a naive Rust translation panic (signed-overflow wrap in `sum += update` and `i * stride`, `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`, the `INT_MAX/9` multiply boundary, out-of-range \"enum-like\" ints).\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 26 rows over the real axes: entry point (low-level `static_sum` *and* `driver`), hidden accumulator state, argument value shape, call-sequence shape/interleaving, `%d` output format shape, fresh-`dlopen` instance.\n\n### Phases B & C — differential tests (`tests/differential.rs`, `tests/common/mod.rs`)\nBoth `.so`s are loaded with `libloading` and driven **only** through `dlsym`'d C symbols, so the `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` wrappers are under test. Every operation is applied to C then Rust under one process-wide mutex, keeping the two hidden accumulators in lockstep; `driver` output is compared byte-for-byte by redirecting **fd 1** to a temp file. Randomized rows use a fixed-seed SplitMix64.\n\n**43 tests (26 configs + 14 errors + 3 symbol/diagnostic), 43 passing, 0 failing.** No divergence was found — `src/lib.rs` needed **no changes** (verified byte-identical to the original).\n\n### Phase D — parity, features, sensitivity\n- `nm -D` diff empty for both the debug and release `.so`.\n- Cargo.toml declares **no `[features]`**, CMakeLists has no options ⇒ one valid combination; `check_features.sh` enumerates the powerset mechanically and runs `cargo check --all-targets` for it plus the default set. `run_tests.sh` runs the suite for {feature combos} × {dev, release} — 43/43 in each.\n- **Mutation check** (to prove the suite isn't vacuous): 5 injected bugs in `src/lib.rs` were each caught by 27–40 tests (`saturating_add`, loop bound 9, `\"%d \\n\"`, `saturating_mul`, accumulator off-by-one), then reverted.\n- **Extra:** the suite also passes against a `-O2`-rebuilt C library (built outside `c_src/`, via `STATICLOOP_C_SO`).\n\nTwo notes on things I added rather than found: `.cargo/config.toml` sets `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1` because the fd-1 capture is process-global (libtest's parallel progress text initially leaked into capture windows and caused 3 spurious failures), and `cargo test` does not build a `cdylib`, so `run_tests.sh` runs `cargo build` explicitly before each `cargo test`. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":589,"cache_read_input_tokens":111311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":589,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc8730bb-4f45-46eb-8140-716d8cf2804e","uuid":"bec426f1-df18-4ae3-a0a2-ab76141a4f4f","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:59:35.861Z"}
